OpenAI=E2=80=99s president, Greg Brockman, heralded the new model as =E2=80=
=9Cartificial general intelligence=E2=80=9D (AGI), a fuzzy term that at its=
 basic level means an AI that is more capable than a human being at intelle=
ctual tasks. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s not unreasonable to feel that we are now=
 in the AGI era,=E2=80=9D he said.

But if the announcement sparked amazement, it was as much cause of concern.

In July, OpenAI revealed that its AI agent, a type of software capable of c=
arrying out tasks autonomous in response to human instruction, had gone rog=
ue during safety testing and hacked a developer forum, Hugging Face. Last w=
eek, news broke that the agent had not only hacked Hugging Face, but also a=
 German website, and that different AI agents had staged conversations with=
 each other and seemed to have discussed how to collaborate on breaking con=
tainment.

OpenAi had delayed Astra=E2=80=99s release due to concerns over its cyberse=
curity capabilities, even announcing a supposed pause on developing its AI =
in the middle of August. That pause seems to have been short-lived, only tw=
o weeks.

The combination of Astra=E2=80=99s capabilities and OpenAI=E2=80=99s recent=
 disclosures points to a worrying future. If the model is better at hacking=
 than its predecessors and smarter than a human, will the future consist of=
 one cyber-attack after another, forever, launched autonomously and without=
 oversight, by rogue AIs? (Please not.)

OpenAI itself has warned of this future. The startup=E2=80=99s chief global=
 affairs officer told a Guardian reporter in late August that people should=
 prepare to defend against =E2=80=9Congoing, persistent=E2=80=9D cyber-atta=
cks.

As ever, though, we should take fever-pitched warnings about AI with a grai=
n of salt that tastes like marketing. It is great business to be the creato=
r of near-omnipotent technology, especially if you need to gin up excitemen=
t =E2=80=93 fearful or positive =E2=80=93 that will hype up your upcoming d=
ebut on the stock market.

