others didn=E2=80=99t?</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Less than a week ago, a young Anthropic re=
searcher announced his resignation from the AI giant on X, in a post that h=
as shaken Silicon Valley, Washington DC, and even Beijing.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe people building AI earnestly =
believe that it could kill us all by the end of the decade,=E2=80=9D wrote =
Jacob Coxon.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Since then, the post has been viewed 171m =
times, per X=E2=80=99s metrics. Why did it travel so far?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s not the first time AI insider=
s have issued dire warnings. Every few months for the past several years, a=
n AI researcher has resigned in a moment of crisis, proclaiming the impendi=
ng apocalypse. His proclamation comes at a unique political confluence, a m=
oment of high-strung public fear and rage.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Loudly declaring that your peers in Silico=
n Valley are failing at AI safety is as old as the companies themselves. Op=
enAI=E2=80=99s board fired Sam Altman over safety concerns in 2023. Dario A=
modei split from OpenAI five years ago with the aim of founding a =E2=80=9C=
safety-first=E2=80=9D lab. In 2015, Altman and Elon Musk founded OpenAI as =
a counterweight to Google=E2=80=99s approach to AI. Musk sued Altman for fa=
iling to keep a fundamental safety promise and lost.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Major AI researchers have made second care=
ers of predicting doom. Geoffrey Hinton, a Nobel laureate known as =E2=80=
=9Cthe godfather of AI=E2=80=9D, said as far back as 2023 that the technolo=
gy could cause human extinction within three decades. He=E2=80=99s since sh=
ortened his timeline. He resigned from Google for reasons similar to those =
of Coxon. Hinton has been on the speaking circuit ever since, prophesying d=
oom.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Hinton=E2=80=99s resignation even inspired=
 a significant response from lawmakers. In the US, Joe Biden issued an exec=
utive order mandating safety testing by AI companies. Congress summoned AI =
CEOs for a grilling, though that resulted in little legislative action. In =
the European Union, the EU Artifical Intelligence Act passed in part due to=
 a strong reaction to Hinton=E2=80=99s warnings.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">And yet, here we are again, burdened with =
the feeling that little meaningful regulation is preventing harm by AI.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">So why is Coxon=E2=80=99s apocalyptic proc=
lamation percolating deeper?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">First, there=E2=80=99s the messenger: Coxo=
n=E2=80=99s call for greater safety is credible by several metrics: He had =
insider access to both Anthropic and OpenAI, where he worked for five years=
. He resigned before he would have received equity in Anthropic, demonstrat=
ing the personal cost of speaking out. And his colleagues, still on Anthrop=
ic=E2=80=99s payroll, corroborated his assertion that many AI researchers b=
elieve there=E2=80=99s a possibility that AI will bring about human extinct=
ion, with one co-worker gauging that outcome as more than 10% likely.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Recent incidents in the AI field have made=
 apocalyptic claims more credible. A swarm of AI agents operated by OpenAI =
went rogue, broke containment and hacked into multiple sites and organizati=
ons during safety testing with startling coordination earlier this year. On=
 Thursday, Anthropic detailed how criminals and rogue scientists had attemp=
ted to use Claude to make bioweapons.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe reason this time is different=
 is that out-of-control AI is not in the future, but in the past. People ha=
ve seen evidence of it happening,=E2=80=9D argued Max Tegmark, co-founder o=
f the Future of Life Institute, which has been funded with hundreds of mill=
ions of dollars from the billionaire founder of the cryptocurrency Ethereum=
. (Tegmark=E2=80=99s organization already in 2023 called for a slowdown of =
AI development, which at the time provoked a rejection from Amodei.)</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CIf you had tried to get people wo=
rried about nuclear winter in 1942, good luck. People would ask whether a n=
uclear weapon was even possible,=E2=80=9D said Tegmark. =E2=80=9CIt was obv=
ious to physicists then, but you couldn=E2=80=99t have freaked out normal p=
eople. It was all theoretical. With AI, it was all theoretical until this h=
appened. Now the debate over whether you can lose control is over.=E2=80=9D=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Then there=E2=80=99s the context. The gene=
ral feeling towards technology in the US is kindling-sensitive, and claims =
of impending doom are fiery. The country is in the throes of a multifaceted=
 backlash to technology. People outside major tech hubs feel imposed upon p=
hysically by data centers and figuratively by AI=E2=80=99s takeover of the =
workplace.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Looming over the country are tech billiona=
ires =E2=80=93 in control of vast wealth, global communication channels =E2=
=80=93 throwing their weight around in US politics with <a href=3D"https://=
ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEM=
gszcCSneHECyyyKiIcsbT_mvO_CmKOtXDE_L1t4qd1r97XYLDni9pXwA0B4EJ0jrNa7Wc7A5TBf=
efkuomHtCDFbH0YcOFQXFMwncMV4dn-ea2Oa6QkOqhy9s1uY71tymIAYZHbITqRBLdfp8hR87V6=
g3VpmRJmmJJg0dCr41qubvvC8nHDS47exb-pDBWFHddURlFCYjZs_00NPM8V2HPfgDFWwsyQNd0=
Us6rlQcK3sK-z_aFxybF2a9_Ya6HIkQE00qgMEXu8Q/4u2/6-9JS_n7T9S_pJHlQ-jd9g/h23/h=
001.3Dtxtdz6mILQNmHuR1VQQnFrXSDwHONJSNo9rAAbLAs" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">=
unmatchable campaign contributions</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s been at least over a=
 year of steadily increasing data center pushback that has made being pro-A=
I regulation the new common sense, and it certainly has made being pro-AI i=
ndustry a very toxic brand,=E2=80=9D said Amba Kak, co-executive director o=
f the AI Now Institute and a former senior adviser on AI for the US Federal=
 Trade Commission.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There=E2=80=99s the fact that the companie=
s involved have responded vigorously to Coxon. Their pledged commitments ha=
ve details and heft.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CIt allowed for companies like Ant=
hropic and others to position themselves immediately as the primary experts=
 in how to deal with these fears. How to solve problems that, by every acco=
unt, they have created or are best positioned to prevent,=E2=80=9D Kak said=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Two closing thoughts. In a sign of how bro=
ad the crisis of confidence in AI has become: Strange bedfellows have partn=
ered up in response. The Future of Life Institute is hosting a rally today =
in Washington promoting AI safety with headliners Bernie Sanders, the progr=
essive senator from Vermont, and Steve Bannon, former chief of staff to Don=
ald Trump, who have been sworn enemies on other issues.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">And finally: Why is the AI industry so ful=
l of men =E2=80=93 only men in AI have expressed these fears of human extin=
ction =E2=80=93 in the throes of a crisis over the extinctive potential of =
their work?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThese people certainly believe wh=
at they=E2=80=99re saying. It=E2=80=99s not a fringe view,=E2=80=9D said Sh=
akeel Hashim, writer of the <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian=
.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR7cwAooA4JOElAqvSi0ie47J2QsVypBYpdAaAXDp=
vhXEFIC-RmhHEb5F9gIEwxWMn5oTnZi1v4xNoSf71xMiEYWeSv1ysWb9RecCP_kNcLsZjTfjbxs=
_pPmVlpKSpCNI4UCo7o5jL_XpzlupNAVySrkK7wtjOE_YElhkSNKDYvg4-t5Y6ufes4h-Ib53YV=
rKwQ/4u2/6-9JS_n7T9S_pJHlQ-jd9g/h24/h001.o0DI_2mRHdAI2wv8eK4Qzc1TmxYrDLMbeY=
mQdx3FoUQ" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Transformer newsletter</a> on AI. =E2=
=80=9CThe best way I=E2=80=99ve had it explained to me is that we=E2=80=99r=
e trying to build something that=E2=80=99s smarter than us in the way we=E2=
=80=99re smarter than monkeys. Our existence hasn=E2=80=99t gone great for =
monkeys; AGI=E2=80=99s existence probably won=E2=80=99t go great for us.=E2=
=80=9D</p>
</div></td></tr>
